course: dictionary
lesson: 12657
title: Dissatisfy and dissatisfied
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word dissatisfy is built from two parts: dis- and satisfy. The part dis- often means not, and satisfy means to please someone or to give them what they want. So to dissatisfy someone means to fail to please them.
explain: «The customer was dissatisfied with the cold pizza.» The customer was not happy, because the pizza was not good enough. Dissatisfied is the form you will see most often. It is an adjective, and it describes how a person feels.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The customer was not pleased with the cold pizza» still makes sense, so dissatisfied means not pleased, or not happy because something is not good enough.
fact: Dissatisfy is a verb. Dissatisfies, dissatisfied and dissatisfying are its other forms.
fact: «Dissatisfied» means not happy because something is not good enough.
fact: «Dissatisfied with» is a common phrase: «dissatisfied with the result».
fact: «Dissatisfying» describes something that makes people unhappy, such as «a dissatisfying ending».
fact: Satisfied is the opposite: happy because something is good enough.
exercise: «The customer was dissatisfied with the cold pizza.» What does dissatisfied mean? | Pleased and full | Excited to order again | *Not happy because the pizza was not good enough | Very hungry
exercise: Mia was ___ with her science mark, so she asked to do the test again. Which word fits? | *dissatisfied | grateful | delighted | cheerful
exercise: «The dissatisfied guests asked for their money back.» Find and copy the word that means not happy. | *dissatisfied | asked | guests | money
test: To dissatisfy someone means to | *Fail to please them | Make them fall asleep | Give them a prize | Please them completely
test: «The new game was dissatisfying for players, who wanted more levels.» What does dissatisfying describe? | Something that makes people laugh | Something that is very fast | *Something that makes people unhappy | Something that is free
exam: Which word means not happy with something because it is not good enough? | pleased | satisfied | cheerful | *dissatisfied
